63870c0f51da2ffcc26ddf3c6c594d243a3282469fbc16661e9b3abf&node=scalar.conditional_rounding&relation=prerequisites","prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=6c394d5e63870c0f51da2ffcc26ddf3c6c594d243a3282469fbc16661e9b3abf&view=arguments&node=scalar.conditional_rounding&assumptions=true"},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=6c394d5e63870c0f51da2ffcc26ddf3c6c594d243a3282469fbc16661e9b3abf&ref=sha256%3Af22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92%2Fnodes%2Fscalar.conditional_rounding","record":{"assumption_ids":["scalar.paper_admissible"],"boundary":"This is a conditional expectation identity, not a claim that F_N equals the terminal gradient pointwise. Independence and the bound |u|≤1 are essential.","citation_ids":["scalar-r2-26-cite-conditional-rounding"],"evidence_ids":[],"id":"scalar.conditional_rounding","kind":"claim","label":"Independent Gaussian rounding preserves the conditional mean","locator":"consequences.tex:107–115,162–170; rounding paragraph","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-consequences","statement":"For fixed 0<T<1,N with finite positive normalizers, define F_N=sgn(u(T,Y_N)+2 Φ_G(Z_{N+1})−1), with Z_{N+1} independent of the first N coordinates and |u|≤1. Then E[F_N|Z₁,…,Z_N]=u(T,Y_N). Its zero set has probability zero, so the value assigned by sign at zero is immaterial.","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.conditional_rounding","relations":[{"derived":true,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.conditional_rounding","id":"field:ccf8a0108edc1ffcc4e718a159a4f9b58cc4de2b8eeaa3639c02e45ec02871b5","kind":"assumption_ids","owner_ref":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f6c8decded774b95a041d92/nodes/scalar.conditional_rounding","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","source_field":"assumption_ids","to":"sha256:f22708f3180068944c06829213f78f6ecfb65ef34f